<title>USA: NO DAMAGING COLD FOR BRAZIL'S COFFEE AREAS - WSC.</title>
<headline>NO DAMAGING COLD FOR BRAZIL'S COFFEE AREAS - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is in sight for Brazil's coffee growing areas during the next five days, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The forecast is for dry weather Thursday and Friday, with low temperatures of 50-65 degrees F.</p>
<p>The outlook for Saturday to Monday is for dry and mild conditions, WSC said.</p>
</text>
